       }
      ],
      "text": "**I’d skip a recreational ride tonight**, especially a hard or long one. The latest Kuching reading I found was **US AQI 133** (unhealthy for sensitive groups), with **PM2.5 at 48.3 µg/m³**; its forecast trends down through the evening but remains around **109 at 7 pm**. Readings can vary by station, so check Malaysia’s DOE/APIMS reading just before you go. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/my-en/air-quality/malaysia/sarawak/kuching))\n\nCycling makes you breathe harder, and EPA guidance at AQI 101–150 advises people who are active outdoors—especially those with asthma or other heart/lung conditions, children, and older adults—to reduce prolonged or heavy exertion. If you must ride, keep it short and easy; don’t go if the haze is obvious or you’re coughing, wheezing, or short of breath. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/sites/default/files/2018-04/aqi_brochure_02_14_0.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nThere’s also a chance of evening thunderstorms and rain in Kuching, so wet-road conditions are another reason to postpone. ([met.gov.my](https://www.met.gov.my/forecast/weather/town/Tn187/?utm_source=openai))",
